# DRAFT-multipledispatch-version-metadata-reconciliation
id: DRAFT-multipledispatch-version-metadata-reconciliation
title: multipledispatch 发行版本与模块 __version__ 双来源校验
software: multipledispatch
version: 1.0.0
phase: package|consumer|review
category: python-metadata
adaptation_path: B
distribution_version: 1.0.0
module_version: 0.6.0
metadata_sources:
  - "importlib.metadata.version('multipledispatch')"
  - "multipledispatch.__version__"
root_cause: setup.py/PyPI metadata was updated independently from module __version__
risk: consumers may read different version sources and silently disagree
solution: retain upstream source, set Conan version to distribution version, assert and document both values
forbid_1: overwrite __version__ during packaging
forbid_1_reason: changes upstream runtime behavior without an adaptation requirement
forbid_2: validate only one version source
forbid_2_reason: hides either packaging metadata drift or module-level compatibility behavior
verification: "consumer test asserts metadata=1.0.0 and module=0.6.0, then exercises dispatch APIs"
applicability: python-distribution-module-version-drift
principles: preserve-upstream-behavior, dual-source-version-check, consumer-visible-evidence
doc_file: knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-multipledispatch-version-metadata-reconciliation.md
